flowchart TB
    accTitle: Export and authenticate an encrypted backup
    accDescr: Export requires authorized vault access and a separate confirmed backup passphrase. Core validates all items, derives a key using PBKDF2-SHA256 and encrypts the entry payload with AES-GCM. The temporary file is authenticated before replacement and the final file afterward. Status recording is a separate paired config update; its failure does not invalidate an already verified backup.
    start["Backup Center: export\nAuthorized desktop vault action"] --> pass{"Backup passphrase confirmed?\n12 to 4096 characters"}
    pass -->|No| reject["Correct input or cancel\nNo backup written"]:::danger
    pass -->|Yes| payload["Validate and serialize entries\nInclude history and Trash"]
    payload --> key["KEY: PBKDF2-SHA256\n600,000 iterations; 16-byte random salt"]:::key
    key --> encrypt["AES-256-GCM encrypt\nPasswordToolBackup v1 envelope"]
    encrypt --> temp["Write temporary file\nin destination directory"]
    temp --> verifyTemp{"Authenticate and validate\nentire temporary backup?"}
    verifyTemp -->|Failure| preserve["Report failure\nPrevious destination preserved"]:::danger
    verifyTemp -->|Success| replace["Replace destination file"]
    replace --> verifyFinal{"Authenticate and validate\nentire final backup?"}
    verifyFinal -->|Failure| distrust["File may exist; do not rely on it\nCreate and verify another backup"]:::danger
    verifyFinal -->|Success| health["Record exported and verified times\nPaired config update"]
    health -->|Success| done["Backup created and verified"]:::good
    health -->|Failure| partial["Backup is verified\nApp status update failed"]:::danger
    classDef key fill:#ffffff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#0f172a,stroke-dasharray:4 3
    classDef danger fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b
    classDef good fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d
